drm/amdgpu: gmc v10: flush PASID TLBs through MMIO on Cyan Skillfish (BC-250)

Not this repository's change. The line is anrp's, given on 2026-05-30 in
https://github.com/ROCm/ROCm/issues/6313 as the workaround for the KIQ-fence
freeze on gfx1013, and confirmed by ahorek on 2026-06-04; this file is that
line in patch form with a comment, kept here so the recipe can apply it. What
the repository adds is the observation that the same line also removes the
compute-queue's silent wrong results, an n=1 A/B in its logs. No author or
sign-off is claimed on the change; see patches/PROVENANCE.md.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -984,7 +984,8 @@ static int gmc_v10_0_hw_init(struct amdgpu_ip_block *ip_block)
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = ip_block->adev;
 	int r;

-	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = !amdgpu_emu_mode;
+	/* BC-250/gfx1013: route PASID TLB flushes via MMIO, not the KIQ ring (ROCm/ROCm#6313) */
+	adev->gmc.flush_pasid_uses_kiq = false;

 	/* The sequence of these two function calls matters.*/
 	gmc_v10_0_init_golden_registers(adev);
